7] [17592186562365 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e1e0f312-cd0e-5c8b-a953-be01ee2625b0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562428 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562298 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562428 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562305 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562428 #edb/ref 1069 "q-208827" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562428 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562428 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-5y=7 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{3}+4y=-\\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the system of equations given above.\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,y=$\n{{field-2}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562428 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "40e64447-ceb6-5045-8392-d608f9b3b14b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562428 #edb/ref 1074 "To get rid of the fractions in the second equation, we must multiply the second equation by the lowest common denominator of the fractions, which is $3.$\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-5y=7 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{3}+4y=-\\frac{8}{3} & |\\,\\times 3\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}x-5y=7 \\\\ 2x+12y=-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will use the substitution method to solve the system. Let's solve for $x$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-5y & =7 \\\\ x & =5y+7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we can substitute $x=5y+7$ into the second equation and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+12y & =-8 \\\\ 2(5y+7)+12y & =-8 \\\\ 10y+14+12y & =-8 \\\\ 22y+14 & =-8 \\\\ 22y & =-22 \\\\ y & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the value of $x,$ we substitute $y=-1$ into the equation $x=5y+7,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =5y+7 \\\\  & =5(-1)+7 \\\\  & =-5+7 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=2,\\,y=-1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562476 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562224 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562476 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562246 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562476 #edb/ref 1069 "q-216312" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562476 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562476 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{4}p+3q=25 \\\\ p+\\frac{2}{5}q=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$p=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,q=$\n{{field-2}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562476 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b1b90563-ce29-5141-8ac6-0ac20bb77c12" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562476 #edb/ref 1074 "To get rid of fractions, we multiply the first equation by $4$ and the second equation by $5,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{4}p+3q=25 & |\\times 4 \\\\ p+\\frac{2}{5}q=0 & |\\times 5\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}5p+12q=100 \\\\ 5p+2q=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will use the elimination method to solve the system. Notice that if we multiply the first equation by $-1,$ then we will get a $-5p$ term that can cancel with the $5p$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}5p+12q=100 & |\\,\\times (-1) \\\\ 5p+2q=0 & \\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}-5p-12q=-100 \\\\ 5p+2q=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations eliminates the $p$-variable, and allows us to solve for $q:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\cancel{-5p}-12q & =-100 \\\\ \\cancel{5p}+2q & =0 \\\\ (-12q+2q) & =(-100+0) \\\\ -10q & =-100 \\\\ q & =\\frac{100}{10} \\\\ q & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $q=10$ into the second equation to solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5p+2q & =0 \\\\ 5p+2\\cdot 10 & =0 \\\\ 5p+20 & =0 \\\\ 5p & =-20 \\\\ p & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system is $p=-4,\\,q=10.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562489 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562281 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562489 #edb/ref 1069 "q-52203" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562489 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562489 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the solution to the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-\\frac{2}{7}y=2 \\\\ -x+\\frac{2}{9}y=2\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562489 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "be4c74c9-6e39-5f39-a1ce-fbc98923b17f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562489 #edb/ref 1074 "To get rid of fractions, we multiply the first equation by $7$ and the second equation by $9,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-\\frac{2}{7}y=2 & |\\times 7 \\\\ -x+\\frac{2}{9}y=2 & |\\times 9\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}7x-2y=14 \\\\ -9x+2y=18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will use the elimination method to solve the system. We can eliminate $y$ by adding the two equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7x-\\cancel{2y} & =14 \\\\ -9x+\\cancel{2y} & =18 \\\\ (7x-9x) & =(14+18) \\\\ -2x & =32 \\\\ x & =-16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $x=-16$ into the first equation to solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7x-2y & =14 \\\\ 7(-16)-2y & =14 \\\\ -112-2y & =14 \\\\ -2y & =126 \\\\ y & =-63\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system is $x=-16$ and $y=-63.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562491 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562365 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562491 #edb/ref 1069 "q-75861" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562491 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562491 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the solution to the  following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{1}{4}y=-1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}x+\\frac{1}{2}y=-6\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562491 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c2c2c978-aae7-58d4-874a-c874d05efc9b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562491 #edb/ref 1074 "To get rid of fractions, we multiply the first equation by $4$ and the second equation by $6,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{1}{4}y=-1 & |\\times 4 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}x+\\frac{1}{2}y=-6 & |\\times 6\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-y=-4 \\\\ 2x+3y=-36\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will use the elimination method to solve the system. Notice that if we multiply the first equation by $-1,$ then we will get a $-2x$ term that can cancel with the $2x$ term in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-y=-4 & |\\,\\times (-1) \\\\ 2x+3y=-36 & \\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x+y=4 \\\\ 2x+3y=-36\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations eliminates the $x$-variable, and allows us to solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\cancel{-2x}+y & =4 \\\\ \\cancel{2x}+3y & =-36 \\\\ (y+3y) & =(4-36) \\\\ 4y & =-32 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{32}{4} \\\\ y & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $y=-8$ into the first equation to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-y & =-4 \\\\ 2x-(-8) & =-4 \\\\ 2x+8 & =-4 \\\\ 2x & =-12 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{12}{2} \\\\ x & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system is $x=-6,\\,y=-8.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562508 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562272 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562508 #edb/ref 1069 "q-26475" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562508 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562508 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the solution to the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2a+3b=-2 \\\\ \\frac{a}{3}-\\frac{b}{6}=-\\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562508 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ef9f41c7-171c-5068-8a8d-ff2c5135b2da" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562508 #edb/ref 1074 "To get rid of the fractions in the second equation, we must multiply the second equation by the lowest common denominator of the fractions, which is $6.$\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2a+3b=-2 \\\\ \\frac{a}{3}-\\frac{b}{6}=-\\frac{5}{3} & |\\,\\times 6\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}2a+3b=-2 \\\\ 2a-b=-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will use the substitution method to solve the system. Let's solve for $b$ in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2a-b & =-10 \\\\ b & =2a+10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we can substitute $b=2a+10$ into the first equation and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2a+3b & =-2 \\\\ 2a+3(2a+10) & =-2 \\\\ 2a+6a+30 & =-2 \\\\ 8a & =-32 \\\\ a & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the value of $b,$ we substitute $a=-4$ into the equation $b=2a+10$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =2a+10 \\\\  & =2(-4)+10 \\\\  & =-8+10 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $a=-4,\\,b=2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562522 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186562553 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562522 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "08d02544-7f45-5298-8142-d17791d03ffa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562522 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186562491 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562526 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2a22f052-de27-5830-aad8-c51679a4477f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562526 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186562476 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562553 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186562526 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562553 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7c82aeb9-8d5e-584a-ac00-f352fd0b7f61" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562553 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186562428 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562574 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186562593 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562574 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "cb4c0ae7-e276-5d26-b075-708ffe0336d8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562574 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186562508 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562593 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186562522 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562593 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "fe6ab4ee-9a03-5db3-9a12-695310a3194a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562593 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186562489 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
